    "sceneId": "s4-forward"
   },
   {
    "start": 18.133,
    "end": 25.733,
    "text": "Every Litefleet node runs six responsibilities. One of them decides whether a SQL statement may run at all.",
    "sceneId": "n-overview"
   },
   {
    "start": 25.733,
    "end": 30.133,
    "text": "The admission engine: per-database lanes, then tenant and node limits.",
    "sceneId": "n-focus"
   },
   {
    "start": 30.133,
    "end": 36.567,
    "text": "Inside the node: Engine.Query, exec.go at release-it/v1-hardened.",
    "sceneId": "s5-into-code"
   },
   {
    "start": 36.567,
    "end": 41.067,
    "text": "Only a single read statement is accepted here; writes go to execute.",
    "sceneId": "s6-read-only"
   },
   {
    "start": 41.067,
    "end": 45.767,
    "text": "admit: the node serves only requests routed with the database's current epoch.",
    "sceneId": "s7-epoch"
   },
   {
    "start": 45.767,
    "end": 50.967,
    "text": "acquire takes a read lane: the per-database bulkhead (2 readers at once).",
    "sceneId": "s8-lane"
   },
   {
    "start": 51.967,
    "end": 56.849,
    "text": "acquire picks the database's read lane, or its single write lane.",
    "sceneId": "n-acquire",
    "stepId": "lane"
   },
   {
    "start": 56.849,
    "end": 65.115,
    "text": "No free lane? Eight statements may wait. The ninth gets 429 tenant_busy at once.",
    "sceneId": "n-acquire",
    "stepId": "wait"
   },
   {
    "start": 65.115,
    "end": 72.499,
    "text": "Next, a tenant slot: four statements per tenant across the node, inside a 250 ms wait.",
    "sceneId": "n-acquire",
    "stepId": "tenant"
   },
   {
    "start": 72.499,
    "end": 80.231,
    "text": "Then a node slot: sixteen per node, or 503 node_busy, handing back what it already holds.",
    "sceneId": "n-acquire",
    "stepId": "node"
   },
   {
    "start": 80.231,
    "end": 85.367,
    "text": "Success returns a release func that frees node, tenant and lane in reverse order.",
    "sceneId": "n-acquire",
    "stepId": "release"
   },
   {
    "start": 85.367,
    "end": 89.867,
    "text": "Rows are scanned from the tenant's SQLite file and streamed as they arrive.",
    "sceneId": "s9-rows"
   },
   {
    "start": 89.867,
    "end": 96.9,
    "text": "Capped at MaxRows (1000) or MaxBytes (1 MiB): the answer says truncated.",
    "sceneId": "s10-caps"
   },
   {
    "start": 96.9,
    "end": 101.267,
    "text": "Capped rows stream back through gateway and HAProxy to the tenant.",
    "sceneId": "s11-reply"
   }
  ],
